#v(1em)

Dear Paul,

I am applying for the DevOps Engineer - Sovereign Cloud Delivery Germany position. Being part of building the foundation for a new, regulated cloud region from the ground up is exactly the kind of technically demanding work I want to be part of.

During my rotations at SAP, I worked hands-on with CI/CD pipelines, Docker, and Git-based workflows, and built production tooling including a VS Code extension using TypeScript and the Language Server Protocol. As co-founder of NEXtickets, I have also operated a live product end-to-end, from infrastructure decisions to actual production incidents, which gave me a real appreciation for what reliable operations require.

I have some hands-on exposure to Terraform from a university project, though I would describe my current level as foundational. Ansible and Kubernetes are not yet part of my daily stack, but I pick up new tools quickly when working on concrete problems, and I am motivated to build deep expertise in cloud operations. I am comfortable in Linux environments and enjoy debugging complex systems.

I finish my dual studies at DHBW Mannheim in September 2026 and hold an unconditional hire recommendation from SAP. I am also open to the security clearance process this role requires.

#v(2em)

Best regards,

#v(0.5em)

*Max Meinel*
